{
  "title": "Ingredient-name worker re-asks every name in a broken batch one at a time",
  "description": "When the model's answer for a multi-name batch is invalid, resolve_batch (server/src/ingredient_names.rs) asks each of the batch's names alone, so one bad name in a full 40-name batch costs 41 calls, spaced by the client's 500ms rate limit (~20s during which the worker resolves nothing else). \
Names that already failed are now asked alone after fresh names, so this only happens on a bad name's first attempt, but that first split is still linear in the batch size. \
Splitting the batch in halves and recursing would find the bad names in about 2*log2(n) calls and resolve the good halves in one call each. \
Seen while fixing the flaky ingredient-name worker tests: at the default rate limit, the tests' deliberately failing names still starved the worker about one run in three.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 4,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "ingredient-names",
  ],
